    {
      "description": "Shows how busy your computer’s brain (CPU) is. Higher values mean more work. If it stays high (>85%) for several minutes, apps may lag. Good for spotting heavy background tasks. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "noValue": "Unavailable"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 20
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\"}[5m])) by (instance)) * 100)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "title": "CPU %",
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 7
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows how much RAM is in use. Higher values mean less free memory for new apps. Sustained high memory usage can cause slowdowns and app switching delays. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "noValue": "Unavailable"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 20
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((node_memory_total_bytes - node_memory_free_bytes - node_memory_inactive_bytes - node_memory_purgeable_bytes) / node_memory_total_bytes * 100)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "title": "Memory %",
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 8
    },
    {
      "description": "Single, easy‑to‑read value. Useful for quick checks and thresholds. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 85
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "noValue": "Unavailable"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "((node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"} - node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"}) / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"} * 100)",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "title": "Disk / %",
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 9
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows internet reliability. Packet loss means some data never arrived. If loss > 2%, video calls and gaming can stutter. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "max": 100,
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent",
          "noValue": "Unavailable"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 20
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "(max(net_ping_loss_percent))",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "title": "Ping Loss",
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 10
    },
    {
      "description": "Shows total internet traffic in and out. Spikes indicate downloads/uploads. Helpful to see if network use is causing slow browsing. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "unit": "Bps",
          "noValue": "Unavailable"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "(sum(rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "RX",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "(sum(rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "TX",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Network Throughput (bytes/s)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "id": 11
    },
    {
      "description": "This panel explains what is happening in simple terms, what to watch for, and why it matters. Missing series are unavailable, not zero. Optional hardware, unmounted disks, stopped VMs and inactive collectors may have no samples.",
